# {{mul-kangxi radical-def}}

====Usage notes====
Do not confuse {{lang-lite|mul|sc=Hani|月}} with {{m-lite|mul|⺼|sc=Hani}}, a form of {{m-lite|mul|sc=Hani|肉||flesh, meat}} when used as the left-hand radical of a character. {{m-lite|mul|⺼|sc=Hani}} is used for parts of the body such as {{m-lite|mul|sc=Hani|背||back}} or {{m-lite|mul|sc=Hani|肝||liver}}. These may be written identically as {{lang-lite|mul|sc=Hani|月}}, but in careful use they are distinguished, with the inside of {{lang-lite|mul|⺼|sc=Hani}} being written with unattached diagonal strokes. This is particularly an issue in looking up characters by radical; compare the [[Appendix:Chinese radical/月|月 index]] and [[Appendix:Chinese radical/肉|肉 index]].

Older/orthodox forms such as the Kangxi dictionary forms may additionally distinguish components that are related to neither {{m-lite|mul|月|sc=Hani}} nor {{m-lite|mul|肉|sc=Hani}}, such as e.g. {{m-lite|mul|朋|sc=Hani}}, {{m-lite|mul|前|sc=Hani}} or {{m-lite|mul|服|sc=Hani}} where the two horizontal strokes {{m-lite|mul|一|sc=Hani}} would be written as two unattached dots {{m-lite|mul|丶|sc=Hani}} instead. Also, the bottom part of {{m-lite|mul|青|sc=Hani}}({{m-lite|mul|靑|sc=Hani}}) components would be written as {{m-lite|mul|円|sc=Hani}}. The orthodox {{lang-lite|mul|sc=Hani|月}} and {{m-lite|mul|⺼|sc=Hani}} components, while similar, would still be distinguished slightly: they both use horizontal strokes, but {{m-lite|mul|⺼|sc=Hani}} connects them to the {{m-lite|mul|⺆|sc=Hani}} shape on both sides, and {{lang-lite|mul|sc=Hani|月}} only connects them on the left side.

