===Etymology 1===
{{ja-kanjitab|つき|yomi=k}}
{{IPAfont|⟨tuki<sub>2</sub>⟩}} → *{{IPAfont|/tukɨ/}} → *{{IPAfont|/t͡sukɨ/}} → {{IPAfont|/t͡suki/}}

From {{inh-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|ojp|月|tr=tuki<sub>2</sub>|sort=つき}}, ultimately from {{inh-lite|ja|jpx-pro|sc=Latinx|*tukuy|sort=つき}}.<ref name="Perard 2012">{{cite-web|first=Thomas|last=Pellard|title=日琉祖語の分岐年代|work=琉球諸語と古代日本語に関する比較言語学的研究」ワークショップ|year=2012|url=http://kikigengo.jp/nishihara/lib/exe/fetch.php?media=library:references:rkoj-pellard.pdf|page=6}}</ref>

Likely a shift from {{inh-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|ojp|月|tr=tuku}}, derived through a fusion with ancient Japanese emphatic nominal particle {{m-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|い|tr=i}}. Compare the development of {{m-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|神|tr=[[kami]]||[[Shinto]] [[deity]]}} from older combining form ''kamu''.

